// valid UTF-8 makes the read fail, and a failed read aborts the program with
// the usual panic message rather than silently mangling the output.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Everything that happens once the output has been captured
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// 1.  The output is echoed to this process' stdout, one println! per line, so
//     a run that produced no output at all prints nothing, a run whose output
//     did not end in a newline still gets one, and carriage returns that were
//     part of a CRLF pair disappear (str::lines strips them).
//
// 2.  With --only-last the output is remembered instead and printed once, when
//     the loop is finished.
//
