//     by a signal has no exit status, and such a run is counted with 99.
//
// 4.  The stop conditions are evaluated.  --until-changes and --until-same
//     compare against the output of the very first run (not against the
//     previous one), while --until-contains and --until-match are applied to
//     each line of the output separately.  --until-success, --until-fail and
//     --until-error look at the exit status only.
//
// 5.  The first run's output is remembered for the two comparisons above.
//
